                          "text":  "I am the second Moon car, and I got the bumpy neighbourhood: the Descartes Highlands, bright hilly country that is older than the dark lunar seas.\n\nJohn Young and Charlie Duke drove me for three days in April 1972, about 27 kilometres in all. Scientists back home expected us to find rocks from ancient volcanoes. We kept finding something else: rocks smashed and stuck back together by enormous impacts. The textbooks had to change.",
